could be shipped): `. ./base.sh`, `. ./variant-a.sh`, `hork__is_converged`, `.
./variant-b.sh`, `hork__is_converged`, `hork__is_converged` -- run `dorc why`
for the per-site detail (the apply runs each anyway, to stay safe)
      [ book.sh:14:1
   14 | . ./base.sh
      | \_________/

   = help:  sm site runs `. ./base.sh`
hint: '.' (line 14) is unmodeled: it is the first wall -- an oracle vouching its convergence would elide it when converged; 5 more unmodeled walls -- dorc why
dorc: run `dorc why` for the per-site cause-chains, or `dorc why book.sh:N` to query a source line
